IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mrcct-member`

-- Military Rehabilitation and Compensation (Consequential and Transitional Provisions) Act 2004 -- worked cases, from the seat
-- of the injured member.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (C2026C00273), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario life raised this Act; the
-- facts are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout. The Commission's determinations are given as facts.
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4 (comparing it with EQUALS does not give FALSE), so
-- the regulative rule is asserted where the trace ends FULFILLED and #TRACEd, with an "-- expect:" line, where it does not.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2. HYPOTHETICAL: Jordan injured a knee in ADF training in 2002; service in 2010 aggravated it. This is au:REQ-0109's
-- question. A claim made on 2 November 2026: the MRCA, for the injury and the aggravation (s 7(1), (2)).
#ASSERT `Which Act governs my claim question` (YearMonthDay 2026 11 2) `the MRCA` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `the MRCA: on and after 1 July 2026 it applies to my injury or disease, and to any aggravation of or material contribution to it, whenever it began and whenever I served (s 7); the DRCA and the VEA are closed to new claims of this kind`
-- Even if Jordan names the DRCA for a claim made after 1 July 2026: the DRCA is closed (DRCA s 14AA), the MRCA applies.
#ASSERT `Which Act governs my claim question` (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) `the DRCA (the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation (Defence-related Claims) Act 1988)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `the MRCA: on and after 1 July 2026 it applies to my injury or disease, and to any aggravation of or material contribution to it, whenever it began and whenever I served (s 7); the DRCA and the VEA are closed to new claims of this kind`
-- Jordan claimed permanent impairment under the DRCA on 3 March 2026, still undecided on 1 July 2026: the DRCA (s 88).
#ASSERT `Which Act governs my claim question` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3) `the DRCA (the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation (Defence-related Claims) Act 1988)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `the DRCA: my claim under it was made before 1 July 2026 and not finally determined by then, so the DRCA continues to govern it, including reconsideration and review (s 88)`
-- The same, but a claim for incapacity compensation: taken to be an MRCA claim (s 93).
#ASSERT `Which Act governs my claim question` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3) `the DRCA (the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation (Defence-related Claims) Act 1988)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `the MRCA: my pending DRCA claim for incapacity compensation is taken to be a claim under section 319 of the MRCA (s 93)`
-- HYPOTHETICAL: Robyn, Vietnam veteran, claimed an increase in her VEA disability pension in May 2026, undecided at 1 July: VEA (s 89).
#ASSERT `Which Act governs my claim question` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 14) `the VEA (the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `the VEA: my claim under it was made before 1 July 2026 and not finally determined by then, so the VEA continues to govern it, including reconsideration and review (s 89)`
-- A pending VEA prisoner of war supplement claim: MRCA (s 110).
#ASSERT `Which Act governs my claim question` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 14) `the VEA (the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `answered` `the MRCA: my pending VEA claim for a prisoner of war payment, or my pending Part VII application, is taken to be a claim or application under the MRCA (ss 110, 112)`
-- An MRCA claim made in 2025 and still pending: the MRCA applies on and after 1 July 2026 (s 7).
#ASSERT `Which Act governs my claim question` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) `the MRCA` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `the MRCA: on and after 1 July 2026 it applies to my injury or disease, and to any aggravation of or material contribution to it, whenever it began and whenever I served (s 7); the DRCA and the VEA are closed to new claims of this kind`
-- Jordan's DRCA claim decided in 2015: the rules then in force are not in this compilation: not covered.
#ASSERT `Which Act governs my claim question` (YearMonthDay 2014 6 1) `the DRCA (the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation (Defence-related Claims) Act 1988)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `my claim was finally determined before 1 July 2026, under the rules then in force (the former Part 2 of this Act), which are not in the deposited compilation and are not encoded`
#ASSERT `Which Act governs my claim question` (YearMonthDay 2010 6 1) `the MRCA` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `my claim was finally determined before 1 July 2026, under the rules then in force (the former Part 2 of this Act), which are not in the deposited compilation and are not encoded`
-- The boundary: 30 June 2026 is before the date of commencement; 1 July 2026 is on it.
#ASSERT `the date of commencement` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1
#ASSERT `Which Act governs my claim question` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) `the VEA (the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `the VEA: my claim under it was made before 1 July 2026 and not finally determined by then, so the VEA continues to govern it, including reconsideration and review (s 89)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 13. Robyn makes an MRCA claim in 2027 for a new condition; she has a VEA defence-caused condition: her old points count.
#ASSERT `Do my old impairment points count question` (YearMonthDay 2027 2 1) TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Commission must determine the impairment points for my old VEA or DRCA condition using the MRCA s 67 guide, and count them towards my total impairment points (s 13(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Do my old impairment points count question` (YearMonthDay 2027 2 1) FALSE EQUALS `no: s 13 applies only to an MRCA claim made on or after 1 July 2026 by a person with a VEA war-caused or defence-caused, or a DRCA, injury or disease`
#ASSERT `Do my old impairment points count question` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE EQUALS `no: s 13 applies only to an MRCA claim made on or after 1 July 2026 by a person with a VEA war-caused or defence-caused, or a DRCA, injury or disease`
-- The rule has no deadline, so it is never FULFILLED by time; it is kept (residual) or breached. Both are traced.
-- expect: BREACH BY the Commission, "s 13(3): ..." (it determined her total without counting the old points)
#TRACE `s 13(2), (3) -- the Commission must determine my old condition's points and count them towards my total` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commission` DOES `determine the impairment points for my old injury or disease using the section 67 guide` AT 10
    PARTY `the Commission` DOES `determine my total impairment points` FALSE AT 20
-- expect: residual (old points determined and counted; the prohibition stands)
#TRACE `s 13(2), (3) -- the Commission must determine my old condition's points and count them towards my total` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commission` DOES `determine the impairment points for my old injury or disease using the section 67 guide` AT 10
    PARTY `the Commission` DOES `determine my total impairment points` TRUE AT 20

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 12(1). Robyn receives a VEA disability pension for her hearing loss: no MRCA permanent impairment compensation for it.
#ASSERT `Can I get MRCA permanent impairment compensation question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: I have already received DRCA (or earlier Act) compensation, or am receiving a VEA pension, for that impairment (s 12(1)); I may still get additional compensation under MRCA s 71 for further impairment from a deterioration`
-- Jordan received a DRCA s 24 lump sum for his knee: likewise.
#ASSERT `Can I get MRCA permanent impairment compensation question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I have already received DRCA (or earlier Act) compensation, or am receiving a VEA pension, for that impairment (s 12(1)); I may still get additional compensation under MRCA s 71 for further impairment from a deterioration`
#ASSERT `Can I get MRCA permanent impairment compensation question` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, so far as this Act goes: s 12(1) does not stop it; whether I qualify is for the MRCA`

-- s 12(2), (3). Jordan was paid DRCA incapacity for 2025 but not for 2027: MRCA for 2027 (s 12(3)); for 2025: no (s 12(2)).
#ASSERT `Can I get MRCA incapacity payments for this period question` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, so far as this Act goes: DRCA payments for other periods do not stop MRCA incapacity payments for this one (s 12(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I get MRCA incapacity payments for this period question` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: I have already received DRCA (or earlier Act) incapacity compensation, or am receiving a VEA pension, for this period and incapacity (s 12(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I get MRCA incapacity payments for this period question` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I have already received DRCA (or earlier Act) incapacity compensation, or am receiving a VEA pension, for this period and incapacity (s 12(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I get MRCA incapacity payments for this period question` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, so far as this Act goes: s 12(2) does not stop it; whether I qualify is for the MRCA`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 92. HYPOTHETICAL: Kai, a former member, was on DRCA incapacity payments on 30 June 2026: MRCA s 118 from the transfer
-- week, no new claim. A Permanent Forces member: s 85. Maintained in hospital under s 22: that continues.
#ASSERT `What happens to my DRCA incapacity payments question` TRUE FALSE `a former member` EQUALS `they move to the MRCA without a new claim: from the transfer week (the first week starting on or after 1 July 2026) I am paid under the MRCA section for my category, and the DRCA still governs weeks that ended before it (s 92(2), (3))` "section 118 of the MRCA, without paragraph 118(1)(d)"
#ASSERT `What happens to my DRCA incapacity payments question` TRUE FALSE `a Permanent Forces member or continuous full-time Reservist` EQUALS `they move to the MRCA without a new claim: from the transfer week (the first week starting on or after 1 July 2026) I am paid under the MRCA section for my category, and the DRCA still governs weeks that ended before it (s 92(2), (3))` "section 85 of the MRCA, without paragraph 85(1)(d)"
#ASSERT `What happens to my DRCA incapacity payments question` TRUE TRUE `a former member` EQUALS `my hospital maintenance continues under section 22 of the old DRCA, and MRCA s 127 does not apply until that stops (s 92(4)); other incapacity payments move to the MRCA from the transfer week (s 92(3))`
#ASSERT `What happens to my DRCA incapacity payments question` FALSE FALSE `a former member` EQUALS `nothing under s 92: it applies only to a person being paid DRCA incapacity compensation immediately before 1 July 2026`
#ASSERT `the MRCA section for my category` `a part-time Reservist` EQUALS "section 86 of the MRCA, without paragraph 86(1)(e)"
#ASSERT `the MRCA section for my category` `a cadet or declared member` EQUALS "section 87 of the MRCA, without paragraph 87(1)(e)"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 12(9), 117. Robyn has VEA treatment for hearing loss and in 2027 becomes entitled to MRCA treatment for a back injury:
-- MRCA for both. Getting VEA treatment for the same condition, no MRCA entitlement yet: VEA for that period.
#ASSERT `Which Act gives me treatment question` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the MRCA, for both: once I become entitled to MRCA treatment for my service injury or disease, I am treated under the MRCA for my separate VEA condition too, and stop being eligible for VEA treatment for it (s 117)`
#ASSERT `Which Act gives me treatment question` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the VEA, for this condition and period: while I am being treated for it under VEA s 85(1) or (2), I am not entitled to MRCA treatment for the same condition and period (s 12(9))`
#ASSERT `Which Act gives me treatment question` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the MRCA, so far as this Act goes: neither s 12(9) nor s 117 moves my treatment`

-- s 14. Robyn's VEA pension under s 13(1)(b) is $1,200 a fortnight and she has no DRCA lump sums: the maximum weekly SRDP
-- falls by $600. Jordan: no VEA pension, DRCA lump sums converting to $45.50 a week: $45.50. Both: $645.50.
#ASSERT `How much is my maximum Special Rate Disability Pension reduced` 1200 0 EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `How much is my maximum Special Rate Disability Pension reduced` 0 45.5 EQUALS 45.5
#ASSERT `How much is my maximum Special Rate Disability Pension reduced` 1200 45.5 EQUALS 645.5
